Hi Team,

We have isolated the Mainframe CPM connectivity issue to DNS canonicalization during TLS validation.

The CPM is configured to connect to:

mvd1.mandtbank.com

However, DNS resolution is canonicalizing this hostname to:

mvd1.intglb4.mtb.com

During the TLS handshake, Windows Schannel is validating the remote certificate against the canonical hostname mvd1.intglb4.mtb.com, which results in Schannel Event ID 36884 because that canonical name is not present in the current certificate SAN.

We have already confirmed:

TCP connectivity to the Mainframe endpoint is successful.

TLS 1.2 negotiation is supported and successful.

The failure occurs specifically during hostname validation.

Another environment does not exhibit the same behavior, which suggests a DNS alias/canonicalization difference.

Could the DNS team please review the record chain for mvd1.mandtbank.com and confirm whether it is intended to canonicalize to mvd1.intglb4.mtb.com?

If this canonicalization is not required, please update the DNS record so the service hostname resolves without introducing a canonical name that differs from the certificate identity.

Once the DNS path is corrected, we can immediately retest CPM connectivity.

Thanks,
Ben
